efine  \n\n   \\[\n   L_i:\\;y = \\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\,x + \\frac{i(k+1-i)-i^2}{k+1-i}\n          = \\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\,x + \\frac{i(k+1-2i)}{k+1-i}.\n   \\]\n\n   *The slope of \\(L_i\\) is \\(\\displaystyle m_i=\\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\).*\n   Because \\(1\\le i\\le k\\) we have \\(0<m_i\\neq 1\\) and \\(m_i\\neq\\infty\\); moreover \\(m_i\\neq -1\\) (the equality \\(i/(k+1-i)=-1\\) would give \\(i=-(k+1-i)\\), impossible for positive integers).  \n   Hence every \\(L_i\\) is **sunny** and the \\(k\\) slopes are pairwise distinct, so the lines are distinct.\n\n   Let \\((a,b)\\in T_k\\); thus \\(1\\le a\\le k\\) and \\(1\\le b\\le k+1-a\\).  \n   Set \\(i=a\\).  Substituting \\(x=a\\) into the equation of \\(L_a\\) gives  \n\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{a}{k+1-a}\\,a + \\frac{a(k+1-2a)}{k+1-a}\n       = \\frac{a^2 + a(k+1-2a)}{k+1-a}\n       = \\frac{a(k+1-a)}{k+1-a}=a .\n   \\]\n\n   Hence the point \\((a,b)\\) lies on \\(L_a\\) **iff** \\(b=a\\).  \n   To obtain the required covering for *all* points we modify the intercepts as follows.\n\n   For each \\(i\\) define a new line  \n\n   \\[\n   \\widehat L_i:\\;y = \\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\,x + c_i,\n   \\qquad\n   c_i = (k+1-i) - \\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\,i .\n   \\]\n\n   By construction \\(\\widehat L_i\\) passes through the point \\((i,\\,k+1-i)\\), i.e. the *outer* diagonal of \\(T_k\\).  \n   Moreover, for any \\((a,b)\\in T_k\\) we have  \n\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{a}{k+1-a}\\,a + c_a\n       = \\frac{a(k+1-a)}{k+1-a}=k+1-a .\n   \\]\n\n   Thus every point of the outer diagonal belongs to exactly one of the lines \\(\\widehat L_i\\) (the one with the same first coordinate).  \n\n   It remains to see that the interior points are also covered.  \n   Take an interior point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(b<k+1-a\\).  \n   Choose the index  \n\n   \\[\n   i = k+1-b\\;( \\;1\\le i\\le k\\;).\n   \\]\n\n   Because \\(b\\le k\\) we have \\(1\\le i\\le k\\).  \n   Substituting \\(x=a\\) into \\(\\widehat L_i\\) gives  \n\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{i}{k+1-i}\\,a +